# tbl-p0064-01: independent pixel inventory FIRST

Recorded immediately after the single original-PNG view and before reading the
candidate exercise or any source-table-FIRST metadata. No prior table metadata,
old page, fig05, other source image, solution, or answer was consulted.

Source: ssot-resources/soviet10year-textbooks/artifacts/7a/figures/tbl-p0064-01.png
Expected SHA-256: 7d74363e688baa48d395105181f028afa73144901551504f0f128ed0a857d285
Original image views at this point: 1. Preview image views: 0.

## Source Facts

- One rectangular ruled table in two stacked bands.
- Upper band: 2 rows, 5 columns; first column is the row-heading column,
  followed by four body columns.
- Lower band: 2 rows, 6 columns; first column is the row-heading column,
  followed by five body columns.
- Each band has a body-name row and a mass row.
- Two distinct horizontal rules make the middle boundary double.
- Outer border, row rules, and all column separators are present. The lower
  column divisions do not coincide with the upper divisions.
- The original row headings are Chinese: body/planet and mass in kilograms.
  The modern SVG must not copy that script.
- Nine masses, with printed mantissas and exponents preserved exactly:

| Band | Column (1-based) | Body | Printed Mass |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Upper | 2 | Mercury | 3.17 x 10^23 |
| Upper | 3 | Venus | 4.87 x 10^24 |
| Upper | 4 | Earth | 5.98 x 10^24 |
| Upper | 5 | Mars | 6.40 x 10^23 |
| Lower | 2 | Jupiter | 1.90 x 10^27 |
| Lower | 3 | Saturn | 5.69 x 10^26 |
| Lower | 4 | Uranus | 8.70 x 10^25 |
| Lower | 5 | Neptune | 1.03 x 10^26 |
| Lower | 6 | Pluto | 5.40 x 10^24 |

The lower band order is Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus, Neptune, Pluto. No sorting or
ratio result is printed in the source. The data are a historical source dataset,
not a statement of present-day measured masses.

## Modern Decisions, Not Source Facts

- Translate body names to the English names above.
- Translate both heading cells to Body and Mass (kg).
- Use clean deterministic geometry and typography; regularize the source's
  hand-scanned uneven rule widths and column widths without changing cell counts.
- Preserve both bands and the double middle rule.
- Typeset powers as superscripts and preserve trailing zeros.
- Instructional scroll display: actual fixed media width 640 px, minimum final
  text size 16 px; no canvas-width-only legibility claim.
- No named points or pointRelationships are meaningful for this table.

## Planned Assertion Mapping

- upper-grid -> upper-grid-dimensions: rows 2, columns 5.
- lower-grid -> lower-grid-dimensions: rows 2, columns 6.
- middle-boundary-top and middle-boundary-bottom: distinct full-width rules.
- Each of the nine entries maps its English body-name object and mass object
  to its source band and column, with explicit label-object count assertions.
- Row headings map to each band's first column.

This is author-side source evidence, not a formal independent review or promotion.
